+# ArbiLend — Security Audit Report
+
+**Scope**: `src/LendingMarket.sol`, `src/CollateralVault.sol`, `src/PriceOracle.sol`, `src/MarketProxy.sol`, `src/interfaces/*` (420 LOC total)
+**Commit**: `8f9a9ce` (working tree clean)
+**Target chain**: Arbitrum One
+**Date**: 2026-08-27
+**Method**: EVM audit checklist sweep — general, precision-math, erc20, defi-lending, proxies, signatures, oracles, chain-specific, dos, access-control
+
+---
+
+## Verdict
+
+**Do not deploy this in two weeks.** Four Critical issues each independently allow a stranger to
+take every dollar in the market, and one of them (C-4) fires with no attacker at all — it
+liquidates honest, ~2x-overcollateralised users on a sub-1% price move. On top of that there is no
+test suite, so none of the fixes below can currently be regression-checked.
+
+The three unprotected setters (C-1, C-2, C-3) are a five-minute fix. C-4 is a one-line fix. Those
+four are what you hand the team on Monday. The High list is the two-week work.
+
