+## [C-3] `setLiquidationThreshold` has no access control
+
+**Severity**: Critical
+**Category**: evm-audit-access-control, evm-audit-defi-lending
+**Location**: `src/LendingMarket.sol:96-99` — `setLiquidationThreshold(uint256)`
+
+**Description**
+Missing `onlyOwner`, and also missing any sanity bound. `liquidationThreshold` is the only term
+separating a healthy position from a liquidatable one (`LendingMarket.sol:150`).
+
+**Proof of Concept — steal 5% of every open position**
+1. Attacker calls `setLiquidationThreshold(0)`.
+2. `healthFactor(user)` is now `(collateral/debt) * 0 * WAD / BPS == 0` for every borrower, so every
+   position is below `WAD`.
+3. Attacker calls `liquidateAll()` (or `liquidate(user)` per victim). For each borrower they repay
+   `debt` USDC and receive collateral worth `debt * 10500 / 10000`.
+4. Net profit: 5% of the entire outstanding debt of the protocol, taken from users who were never
+   undercollateralised. Flash-loanable, since repay and seize happen in the same transaction.
+
+**Proof of Concept — borrow at 100% LTV**
+Set `liquidationThreshold` to a large value, deposit $1M of wstETH, borrow $1M USDC (`healthFactor`
+is satisfied whenever `collateral >= debt`, see C-4), abandon the position. Net theft of the
+difference.
+
+**Recommendation**
+Add `onlyOwner` and bound the value. Also call `accrueInterest()` first, as `setBorrowRate` correctly
+does at `LendingMarket.sol:102`, so the change does not retroactively reprice accrued interest:
+
+```solidity
+uint256 internal constant MAX_LIQUIDATION_THRESHOLD = 9_000;
+
+function setLiquidationThreshold(uint256 bps) external onlyOwner {
+    if (bps == 0 || bps > MAX_LIQUIDATION_THRESHOLD) revert InvalidThreshold(bps);
+    accrueInterest();
+    liquidationThreshold = bps;
+    emit LiquidationThresholdUpdated(bps);
+}
+```
+
+Note that lowering the threshold instantly makes existing positions liquidatable with no warning;
+this parameter in particular should be timelocked so borrowers have time to top up.
+
