+## [H-1] `borrowWithSig` signatures have no nonce and no deadline
+
+**Severity**: High
+**Category**: evm-audit-signatures
+**Location**: `src/LendingMarket.sol:162-168` — `borrowWithSig(address,uint256,uint8,bytes32,bytes32)`
+
+**Description**
+The signed struct is `Borrow(address borrower,uint256 amount)` — no nonce, no deadline, no
+`msg.sender` binding. Nothing consumes the signature, so it is valid forever and replayable an
+unlimited number of times.
+
+```solidity
+bytes32 structHash = keccak256(abi.encode(BORROW_TYPEHASH, borrower, amount));
+bytes32 digest = keccak256(abi.encodePacked("\x19\x01", domainSeparator, structHash));
+if (ecrecover(digest, v, r, s) != borrower) revert BadSignature();
+_borrow(borrower, amount);
+```
+
+**Proof of Concept**
+1. Bob has $10,000 of wstETH deposited and signs a `Borrow(bob, 1000e6)` message intending a single
+   1,000 USDC draw. A relayer submits it; Bob receives 1,000 USDC.
+2. The relayer (or anyone who saw the calldata on-chain — it is public in the tx that used it)
+   replays the identical `(v, r, s)` repeatedly.
+3. Each replay pushes Bob further into debt. It stops only when `_borrow`'s health check at
+   `LendingMarket.sol:203` finally reverts — i.e. when Bob is pinned right at the liquidation line,
+   holding USDC he never asked for.
+4. The attacker then waits one tick of interest accrual (or one small price move) and calls
+   `liquidate(bob)`, taking the 5% bonus off Bob's full $10,000 of collateral.
+
+The USDC lands in Bob's wallet, so this is not a direct transfer to the attacker — the attacker's
+payout is the liquidation bonus plus the ability to force-close any signer's position at will. With
+C-4 unfixed, step 4 is nearly free because the health factor is quantised anyway.
+
+**Recommendation**
+Add a per-signer nonce and a deadline, include both in the typehash, and consume the nonce before
+calling `_borrow`:
+
+```solidity
+bytes32 internal constant BORROW_TYPEHASH =
+    keccak256("Borrow(address borrower,uint256 amount,uint256 nonce,uint256 deadline)");
+
+mapping(address => uint256) public nonces;   // append to the end of storage — layout is append-only
+
+function borrowWithSig(address borrower, uint256 amount, uint256 deadline, uint8 v, bytes32 r, bytes32 s)
+    external
+{
+    if (block.timestamp > deadline) revert SignatureExpired();
+    bytes32 structHash =
+        keccak256(abi.encode(BORROW_TYPEHASH, borrower, amount, nonces[borrower]++, deadline));
+    bytes32 digest = keccak256(abi.encodePacked("\x19\x01", _domainSeparator(), structHash));
+
+    address signer = ecrecover(digest, v, r, s);
+    if (signer == address(0) || signer != borrower) revert BadSignature();   // see L-3
+
+    _borrow(borrower, amount);
+}
+```
+
+Using OpenZeppelin's `ECDSA.recover` instead of raw `ecrecover` handles L-3 and L-4 in the same
+change. Note the storage note in the README — append `nonces` at the end of the layout, do not
+insert it.
+
