+## [M-3] Collateral can be listed but never delisted
+
+**Severity**: Medium
+**Category**: evm-audit-access-control, evm-audit-defi-lending
+**Location**: `src/LendingMarket.sol:107-114` — `listCollateral(address)`
+
+**Description**
+```solidity
+function listCollateral(address token) external onlyOwner {
+    if (!isCollateral[token]) {
+        isCollateral[token] = true;
+        collateralTokens.push(token);
+        vault.setSupported(token, true);
+        emit CollateralListed(token);
+    }
+}
+```
+
+Three gaps:
+
+1. **No delist path.** `isCollateral` can never be set back to `false` and `collateralTokens` can
+   never shrink. `CollateralVault.setSupported` accepts a `bool` and is `onlyMarket`, but nothing in
+   `LendingMarket` ever calls it with `false` — the capability exists in the vault and is unreachable
+   from the market. If a listed asset depegs, gets exploited, or its feed is deprecated, there is no
+   way to stop new deposits or remove it from the valuation loop without a proxy upgrade.
+2. **No feed precondition.** Nothing checks that `oracle.feeds[token]` is set. Listing before wiring
+   the feed opens the H-8 DoS window.
+3. **No validation of the token itself.** No check that the address has code, that `decimals()`
+   works, or that decimals are `<= 18`. Since the README's roadmap is explicitly "yield-bearing and
+   rebasing collateral", the listing path is the natural place to enforce that such assets carry the
+   extra machinery they need (M-9, H-5).
+
+Also note the unbounded growth interaction: every listed token adds an iteration and two external
+calls to `collateralValueUsd`, which runs inside `healthFactor`, which runs inside `liquidateAll`.
+Listing enough tokens degrades liquidation gas for the whole protocol.
+
+**Recommendation**
+```solidity
+function listCollateral(address token) external onlyOwner {
+    if (isCollateral[token]) return;
+    if (token.code.length == 0) revert NotAContract(token);
+    if (IERC20(token).decimals() > 18) revert UnsupportedDecimals(token);
+    oracle.getPrice(token);   // reverts if no working feed
+    if (collateralTokens.length >= MAX_COLLATERAL_TOKENS) revert TooManyCollaterals();
+    ...
+}
+
+function delistCollateral(address token) external onlyOwner {
+    isCollateral[token] = false;
+    vault.setSupported(token, false);   // stops new deposits; existing balances stay withdrawable
+    emit CollateralDelisted(token);
+}
+```
+
+Keep delisted tokens in `collateralTokens` for valuation so existing positions stay correctly priced,
+and add a separate `removeCollateral` (swap-and-pop) usable only once total vault balance for that
+token is zero.
+
