+## [L-1] `repay` always leaves 1 wei of dust principal
+
+**Severity**: Low
+**Category**: evm-audit-precision-math
+**Location**: `src/LendingMarket.sol:170-181` — `repay(address,uint256)`
+
+**Description**
+```solidity
+uint256 debt = debtOf(user);              // floor(principal * index / WAD)
+if (amount > debt) amount = debt;
+debtAsset.transferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), amount);
+principalOf[onBehalfOf] -= amount * WAD / borrowIndex;   // floors again
+```
+
+Both `debtOf` and the principal reduction floor. Repaying the full `debt` reduces principal by
+`floor(floor(p·I/W)·W/I)`, which equals `p - 1` whenever `p·I` is not an exact multiple of `WAD` —
+i.e. essentially always.
+
+So a user who repays their entire stated debt is left with 1 wei of scaled principal, which
+`debtOf` reports as 1 wei of USDC debt. The position can never be closed. `NothingBorrowed` never
+fires. The user stays in the `borrowers` array forever (M-6), accruing interest on dust and costing
+a `healthFactor` evaluation on every `liquidateAll()`. It is also user-visible as a loan that refuses
+to go to zero.
+
+**Recommendation**
+Snap to zero when the user repays in full:
+
+```solidity
+uint256 principalRepaid = amount * WAD / borrowIndex;
+if (amount == debt || principalRepaid >= principalOf[onBehalfOf]) {
+    principalOf[onBehalfOf] = 0;
+    _removeBorrower(onBehalfOf);
+} else {
+    principalOf[onBehalfOf] -= principalRepaid;
+}
+```
+
