+
+## [L-2] `borrow` rounding favours the borrower
+
+**Severity**: Low
+**Category**: evm-audit-precision-math
+**Location**: `src/LendingMarket.sol:201` — `_borrow`
+
+**Description**
+`principalOf[borrower] += amount * WAD / borrowIndex` rounds **down**, so the recorded principal is
+slightly less than the amount actually lent. The rounding direction should favour the protocol on the
+way in and the protocol on the way out; here it favours the user on both. Per-call the loss is at
+most 1 wei of principal, but it is free and repeatable — a user can borrow in many small increments
+to accumulate it.
+
+At the current index magnitude the total extractable value is negligible, which is why this is Low.
+It becomes more material as `borrowIndex` grows over years.
+
+**Recommendation**
+Round up on borrow, keep rounding down on repay credit:
+
+```solidity
+principalOf[borrower] += (amount * WAD + borrowIndex - 1) / borrowIndex;
+```
+
