+## [L-3] `ecrecover` return of `address(0)` is not checked
+
+**Severity**: Low
+**Category**: evm-audit-signatures
+**Location**: `src/LendingMarket.sol:165` — `borrowWithSig`
+
+**Description**
+```solidity
+if (ecrecover(digest, v, r, s) != borrower) revert BadSignature();
+```
+
+`ecrecover` returns `address(0)` for malformed input rather than reverting. An attacker passing
+`borrower = address(0)` with arbitrary `v, r, s` satisfies the equality and reaches
+`_borrow(address(0), amount)`.
+
+**Impact is currently blocked**, honestly: `_borrow` calls `debtAsset.transfer(address(0), amount)`,
+and Circle's USDC implementation reverts on transfers to the zero address, so the whole transaction
+unwinds — including the `borrowers.push(address(0))`. So there is no exploitable path with the
+launch configuration. It is listed because it is a one-line fix, because it stops being blocked if
+`debtAsset` ever changes, and because the check belongs there regardless.
+
+**Recommendation**
+```solidity
+address signer = ecrecover(digest, v, r, s);
+if (signer == address(0) || signer != borrower) revert BadSignature();
+```
+
+Or use OpenZeppelin's `ECDSA.recover`, which reverts on `address(0)` and on malleable `s`, covering
+L-4 at the same time.
+
