+## [L-4] Signature malleability: raw `ecrecover` with no `s` bound
+
+**Severity**: Low
+**Category**: evm-audit-signatures
+**Location**: `src/LendingMarket.sol:162-168` — `borrowWithSig`
+
+**Description**
+`v`, `r` and `s` are passed straight to `ecrecover` with no validation. For any valid signature there
+is a second `(v', r, s')` with `s' = n - s` that recovers the same address. Nothing in the contract
+tracks used signatures, so malleability adds nothing to the replay problem that H-1 does not already
+create — but it will matter the moment a nonce or a used-signature mapping is introduced, since a
+malleated variant would bypass a naive `usedSignature[keccak256(sig)]` guard.
+
+**Recommendation**
+Fix alongside H-1. Enforce the lower half-order bound and valid `v`, or just use
+`ECDSA.recover(digest, v, r, s)`:
+
+```solidity
+if (uint256(s) > 0x7FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF5D576E7357A4501DDFE92F46681B20A0) revert BadSignature();
+if (v != 27 && v != 28) revert BadSignature();
+```
+
